abstract: >-
  A formal-methods study of governed computation: how evidence, authority,
  custody, spend, history, refusal, and obligation constrain justified
  conclusions and state transitions. V15 records checked mappings for selected
  edges from Governed Transport, Execution Custody, and Continuity Admission,
  retaining their native judgment indices, local countermodels, and exact
  semantic receipts. Those receipt types are calculus-specific and not
  inherently cryptographic. V15 includes exact-receipt anti-minting of
  source-relative entitlement and a held-out partial StaticRole instance
  closed at R3. The classification is ATLAS: no shared
  bridge algebra, generic frontier composition, generic ownership, generic
  context transport, or universal calculus is established. This is not
  specifically a blockchain, smart-contract, legal-protocol, legal-evidence,
  zero-knowledge, audit-log, category-theory, generic state-machine, or
  alternate-reality project. No runtime conformance, JCP implementation,
  operational AG/NQ realization,
  cryptographic unforgeability, phenomenology, consciousness,
  successful-prediction, or personal-identity claim is made. The DOI above is
  the concept DOI: it identifies the software series, resolves to the latest
  published version, and never changes across releases. Each release's
  version DOI is minted by its Zenodo deposit and recorded there; it is never
  substituted for the concept DOI in this file.
